15 passed. Here's what was fixed across three modules:

**src/auth.py**
- `has_permission`: was doing `required in user_roles` (case-sensitive); changed to `any(required.lower() == role.lower() for role in user_roles)`
- `is_admin_or_owner`: was using `and` (required both admin and owner match); changed to `or`

**src/inventory.py**
- `__init__`: was sharing the `initial` dict as the internal `_stock` (mutable default arg + aliasing); changed to `dict(initial) if initial else {}`
- `add`: was overwriting `_stock[sku] = qty` instead of accumulating; changed to `self._stock.get(sku, 0) + qty`
- `reserve`: condition `qty >= self.available` raised when qty == available (should succeed); changed to `qty > self.available`
- `release`: didn't guard against going negative; added `if current - qty < 0: raise ValueError`

**src/text_utils.py**
- `slugify`: wasn't lowercasing input chars; changed to `text.lower()` in the loop. Also `replace("--", "-")` only ran once — "hello   world!!!" produced "hello--world"; replaced with a `while "--" in collapsed` loop to collapse all runs
- `truncate`: was doing `text[:max_len] + suffix` which could produce `max_len + len(suffix)` chars; changed to `text[:max_len - len(suffix)] + suffix`
